WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:04.719
Scrooge gasped and sat up.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.837
The wooden bedpost was on his own bed—he was back in his bedroom!

3
00:00:10.838 --> 00:00:16.362
He leaped out of bed, eager to make amends for his past behavior.

4
00:00:16.363 --> 00:00:22.200
"Oh, Jacob Marley, thank you for this precious lesson!" he thought.

5
00:00:22.201 --> 00:00:32.095
"I am still here and alive, which means I still have time to change my future. I know I can do it!"

6
00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:38.370
Scrooge was so overwhelmed by all his new emotions that he could barely dress himself.

7
00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:43.575
He turned his garments inside out, and then started to put them on upside down.

8
00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.413
He even tore a hole in one of his best socks.

9
00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:54.762
"I don't know what to do!" he said, laughing and crying at the same time.

10
00:00:54.763 --> 00:01:05.847
"I feel as light as a feather. I am as happy as an angel and as merry as a schoolboy.

11
00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:08.907
A merry Christmas to everybody!

12
00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:13.700
A happy new year to everyone in the world!"

13
00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:19.017
He ran into his sitting room and looked around at the familiar surroundings.

14
00:01:19.018 --> 00:01:25.530
Instead of seeing the dull apartment of a selfish man, he now saw only wonder and beauty.

15
00:01:25.531 --> 00:01:34.125
"There's the lovely cup that held my tea!" he said, dancing around the room.

16
00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:40.210
"There are the door and chair that the ghost of Jacob Marley used.

17
00:01:40.211 --> 00:01:47.798
Oh, and there's the spot where that giant, the Ghost of Christmas Present, sat!

18
00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:53.505
It's all true. It all really happened."

19
00:01:53.506 --> 00:02:01.025
He laughed loudly, the first genuine laugh he'd let out in many years.

20
00:02:01.026 --> 00:02:05.465
"I don't know what day of the month it is," Scrooge thought.

21
00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:09.350
"I don't know how long I was among the three spirits.

22
00:02:09.351 --> 00:02:15.194
I don't know anything, so I am like a newborn baby.

23
00:02:15.195 --> 00:02:23.454
And I'd much rather be this innocent baby than the awful man I was before."

24
00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:28.844
Just then he heard the church bells ring out the hour.

25
00:02:28.845 --> 00:02:35.241
He ran to the window and yanked it open so he could hear the glorious bells more clearly.

26
00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:40.919
Sticking his head outside, he saw that the morning was bright and clear.

27
00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:46.907
Sunlight washed everything below in a beautiful golden glow.

28
00:02:46.908 --> 00:02:51.755
Then Scrooge spotted a boy, dressed in his best clothes.

29
00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:58.307
"You there!" Scrooge called. "Tell me, what's today?"

30
00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:05.752
The boy looked up with a confused expression. "Pardon me, sir?"

31
00:03:05.753 --> 00:03:13.508
"What day is it, my fine fellow?" Scrooge asked. "Tell me the date!"

32
00:03:13.509 --> 00:03:18.439
"Why, it's Christmas Day, of course," the boy said.

33
00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:25.031
"Christmas Day!" Scrooge said, now speaking to himself rather than the boy.

34
00:03:25.032 --> 00:03:32.955
"So, I haven't missed it. The spirits did all their work in one short night!"

35
00:03:32.956 --> 00:03:39.938
Noticing the boy giving him an odd look, Scrooge added, "I'd like to request a favor.

36
00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:47.498
Do you know the meat shop around the corner, the one with the large turkey hanging in the window?"

37
00:03:47.499 --> 00:03:51.860
"Yes, I know that shop," the boy said.

38
00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:56.471
"What an intelligent boy!" Scrooge said.

39
00:03:56.472 --> 00:04:02.992
"A remarkable boy! Do you know whether they've sold that fine bird yet?

40
00:04:02.993 --> 00:04:08.713
Not the smaller ones—I'm only interested in the big one."

41
00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:13.625
"I just passed by and it's hanging there now," the boy said.

42
00:04:13.626 --> 00:04:18.459
"Wonderful!" Scrooge beamed with delight.

43
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.902
"Go and fetch the owner of the shop and bring him here.

44
00:04:22.903 --> 00:04:26.029
Tell him I want to buy that turkey.

45
00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:32.571
When he arrives, I'll pay him and instruct him where he should deliver it."

46
00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:36.724
The boy still looked confused.

47
00:04:36.725 --> 00:04:43.639
"Come back with the man," Scrooge said, "and I'll give you a few coins.

48
00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:50.288
Come back with him in less than five minutes and I'll give you even more money!"

49
00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:55.083
Swiftly understanding that offer, the boy took off like a shot.

50
00:04:55.084 --> 00:05:00.284
Scrooge watched him go, smiling with pleasure.

51
00:05:00.285 --> 00:05:06.745
"I'll send the turkey to Bob Cratchit's house, and the family won't know who sent it."

52
00:05:06.746 --> 00:05:10.719
He rubbed his hands together gleefully.

53
00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:19.328
"They'll never be able to eat it all. Why, it's twice the size of Tiny Tim!"

54
00:05:19.329 --> 00:05:22.366
Soon the shopkeeper arrived.

55
00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:27.958
He was out of breath and looked as confused as the boy had looked at first.

56
00:05:27.959 --> 00:05:33.866
Scrooge was all smiles when he paid the boy for his errand.

57
00:05:33.867 --> 00:05:37.667
He chuckled out loud when he paid the man for the turkey.

58
00:05:37.668 --> 00:05:43.416
And he laughed even more joyfully when he gave extra money to the shop owner.

59
00:05:43.417 --> 00:05:49.733
That was to pay for the cab that would transport the large bird across town.

60
00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:56.510
With these tasks accomplished, Scrooge changed into his best clothes.

61
00:05:56.511 --> 00:05:59.695
Then he set out into the London streets.

62
00:05:59.696 --> 00:06:10.110
For the first time since childhood, he was about to enjoy Christmas.

